„­bible_version£KJV¤book.§chapter¨sections•…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHaving therefore these promises, dearly beloved, let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙWReceive us; we have wronged no man, we have corrupted no man, we have defrauded no man.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙlI speak not this to condemn you: for I have said before, that ye are in our hearts to die and live with you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙGreat is my boldness of speech toward you, great is my glorying of you: I am filled with comfort, I am exceeding joyful in all our tribulation.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒFor, when we were come into Macedonia, our flesh had no rest, but we were troubled on every side; without were fightings, within were fears.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`Nevertheless God, that comforteth those that are cast down, comforted us by the coming of Titus;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃand not by his coming only, but by the consolation wherewith he was comforted in you, when he told us your earnest desire, your mourning, your fervent mind toward me; so that I rejoiced the more.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«For though I made you sorry with a letter, I do not repent, though I did repent: for I perceive that the same epistle hath made you sorry, though it were but for a season.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«Now I rejoice, not that ye were made sorry, but that ye sorrowed to repentance: for ye were made sorry after a godly manner, that ye might receive damage by us in nothing.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙrFor godly sorrow worketh repentance to salvation not to be repented of: but the sorrow of the world worketh death.¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚ5For behold this selfsame thing, that ye sorrowed after a godly sort, what carefulness it wrought in you, yea, what clearing of yourselves, yea, what indignation, yea, what fear, yea, what vehement desire, yea, what zeal, yea, what revenge! In all things ye have approved yourselves to be clear in this matter.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÃWherefore, though I wrote unto you, I did it not for his cause that had done the wrong, nor for his cause that suffered wrong, but that our care for you in the sight of God might appear unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book.§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ–Therefore we were comforted in your comfort: yea, and exceedingly the more joyed we for the joy of Titus, because his spirit was refreshed by you all.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯For if I have boasted any thing to him of you, I am not ashamed; but as we spake all things to you in truth, even so our boasting, which I made before Titus, is found a truth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And his inward affection is more abundant toward you, whilst he remembereth the obedience of you all, how with fear and trembling ye received him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ@I rejoice therefore that I have confidence in you in all things.¦layout ªlast_verse